    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.70) remains our primary engine, leveraging an elite matchup against Nick Martinez. Despite a slight park penalty, his ability to contribute across all categories\u2014specifically his 62% SB conversion expectation\u2014keeps him anchored in the utility spot. He is joined at the top of the board by **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Luis Arraez** (66.78). Both benefit from favorable SP xERAs near 4.90, with **Dylan Beavers** capitalizing on an elite park factor and leadoff positioning that significantly elevates his run-scoring ceiling. **Jonathan Aranda** (65.77) also grades out as a strong play; his matchup against Bibee is one of our highest-conviction scenarios, as the dynamic platoon advantage and a move into the two-hole position the high-OBA infielder for maximum efficiency.\n\nWe faced a difficult choice in the outfield, ultimately benching **Bryce Harper** (54.04) despite his pedigree. While **Bryce Harper** maintains a solid xwOBA, his struggle against the handedness profile of the opposing starter today lowered his efficiency score just enough to be squeezed out by **Daulton Varsho** (63.04) and **Taylor Ward** (63.35), both of whom are projected for superior production in their respective hitter-friendly environments. The matchup for **Taylor Ward** is particularly noteworthy, as the park factor provides a 16% boost to his base projection, offsetting his unfavorable platoon split. Meanwhile, **Yainer Diaz** (44.38) and **Cal Raleigh** (47.10) remain our most precarious spots; both face tough arms with sub-3.70 xERAs. While these scores are near our floor, we are opting to start them to manage our weekly game caps, though they carry the highest risk of underperformance if the starting pitchers maintain control of the zone.",
